cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite the exact public commit for this research disclosure."
title: "The proper hat-guessing number of K6-e"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: "Protti"
    given-names: "Matthew"
version: "0.1"
date-released: 2026-09-03
repository-code: "https://github.com/matthewprotti/proper-hat-guessing-k5-minus-e"
abstract: >-
  We prove that the proper hat-guessing number of the complete graph on six
  vertices with one edge removed is ten. The lower bound uses an explicit
  deletion-and-repair construction from a sharply four-transitive eleven-point
  permutation group and a Hall-completion criterion. We also classify all
  repairable orbit labels and prove an even-n obstruction for set-symmetric
  line-permutation twin rules.
keywords:
  - hat guessing
  - proper coloring
  - graph theory
  - Hall's theorem
  - Mathieu group
  - combinatorial design
  - AI-assisted mathematics
